ay mr johnson's time is up and  are calling for an election now  changing one man at the top of the tory  party won't make any difference he won't  fix the problems let's have a fresh  start for britain let's have a real  change of government last month boris  johnson narrowly survived a vote of  confidence in his leadership  technically he's immune from another  such challenge for a year but tory  rebels could try and use elections to  the 1922 committee of tory back benches  to change the rules tamara cohen sky  news westminster
 

